      "titre": "File:Snowboard gloves with integrated wrist protection.jpg",
      "description": "Snowboard gloves with integrated wrist protection. The left glove is partly dismantled to show the removable rigid plastic element which is in a pouch on the back of the hand/glove. The ca. 15 cm long and 3 cm wide, quite rigid plastic element is in a pouch on the back of the hand. With the velcro strap, this element is tightly fixated to the wrist, such that the wrist has a reduced freedom to be bent upwards - in this way, the wearer is protected against one of the most common injuries while snowboarding, which happens when the boarder falls to the front and tries to dampen the impact by fall",
